  "description": "PERXOD crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H122 Dy8 N16 O40 2+,8(C1 H4 O1),2(C1 H3 O1 1-),C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.574-3.826 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.66-115.94°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(L2)4(μ3-O)2(CH3O)6(NO3)4(CH3OH)6(H2O)2]·6CH3OH·CH3CN·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
